 Saved the user's provided HTML certificate code to `IIC_Certificate_Generator.html` and fixed a broken JS upload function.\n*   **Logo Image Processing:** Processed all 7 logos using Python `PIL`. Cropped out 50px solid black bars from the left and right sides of `naac.png`. Replaced white backgrounds (RGB > 235) with transparency for all logos to ensure clean rendering.\n*   **Logo Injection & Layout:** Injected the 7 cleaned logos directly into the HTML as Base64 encoded strings to make the file standalone. Structured the header `.logo-strip` into a 3-1-3 flexbox layout (3 left, 1 center, 3 right).\n\n### 4. Model Knowledge\n*   **HTML DOM Regex Issue:** When using python `re.sub` on HTML with `.*?` (and `re.DOTALL`), be extremely careful. An earlier regex swallowed a closing `</div>`, breaking the flexbox layout and hiding all text. Had to use strict `re.compile` with explicit capture groups `(</div>)` to restore the DOM structure.\n*   **Powershell / Python execution:** Running `python -c \"...\"` from PowerShell can fail if there are inline quotes or `$`/`@` characters. Best practice is using a PowerShell Here-String `@\"\"@` saved to a temporary python file, then executing it (e.g., `Set-Content -Path fix.py -Value $code; python fix.py`).\n*   **Image Processing (PIL):** `naac.png` has 50px of solid black on the left and right edges. It was successfully cropped using `img.crop((50, 0, w-50, h))`. White background removal works reliably via `getdata()` replacing pixels `> (235,235,235)`.\n*   **CSS Mix-blend-mode Failure:** Do not use `mix-blend-mode: multiply` for removing backgrounds on the certificate if the source images have innate transparency or black artifacts, as it causes massive visual glitches (turned NAAC borders solid black). Base64 injected PNGs with proper alpha channels generated via Python PIL are strictly better here.\n\n### 5. Files and Code\n*   **Edited/Created Files:**\n    *   `C:\\Users\\prsnl\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\d1b69639-194